note units: stats
note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note stats-payback: payback with END round trips (K17), on globals stpay reads. Two groups, each
note BEGIN, QUERY, SET, QUERY; full and delta (arm 4) have equal start-to-ready and request round
note trips, so every pre-END (full - arm) difference is 0. acq(delta) = 150 ns.
note  p1 (integrator counterexample): full END 100 ns per rep in group 0, arm END 0, so END
note     savings 300 after group 0: payback is 2 QUERYs (after the group's last QUERY), never 0.
note  p2 the same savings only in group 1: payback 4.
note  p3 savings 150 (not above acq): never (2^64 - 1).
note  p4 a request saving at group 0's first QUERY (full 900 instead of 500 ns, 3 reps): 1.
note Exit 0 = pass; otherwise the failing check's code.

note two groups of 4 requests, equal costs for arms 1 and 4, END 0, acq(4) = 150
fn tpbase to void
streset
put STNG 0 2
for g ulong 2
put STGO g mul g 4
put STGN g 4
end
for i ulong 8
k = rem i 4
if eq k 0
put STRO i 1
end
if eq k 2
put STRO i 3
end
if or eq k 1 eq k 3
put STRO i 2
end
end
for r ulong 3
for g ulong 2
for a ulong 2
x = add mul add mul add mul a 3 1 3 r 128 g
put STPR x 1000
put STPE x 0
end
end
for i ulong 8
for a ulong 2
put STRT add mul add mul add mul a 3 1 3 r 65536 i 500
end
end
end
put STAA 4 150
end

note full's END for group g, every rep, = e
fn tpend g ulong e ulong to void
for r ulong 3
put STPE add mul add 3 r 128 g e
end
end

fn main to int
tpbase
tpend 0 100
if ne stpay 4 2
ret 1
end
tpbase
tpend 1 100
if ne stpay 4 4
ret 2
end
tpbase
tpend 0 50
if ne stpay 4 18446744073709551615
ret 3
end
tpbase
tpend 0 100
for r ulong 3
put STRT add mul add 3 r 65536 1 900
end
if ne stpay 4 1
ret 4
end
ret 0
end
